<article class="env-remark" id="02WG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02WG">Remark <span data-tag="02WG">65.4.2</span>.</a> Of the properties of morphisms which are stable under base change (as listed in Remark <a href="/tag/02WF" data-tag="02WF">65.4.1</a>) the following are also <em>stable under compositions</em>: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
closed, open and locally closed immersions, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02V0" data-tag="02V0">26.24.3</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
quasi-compact, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01K6" data-tag="01K6">26.19.4</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universally closed, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01W3" data-tag="01W3">29.42.4</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(quasi-)separated, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01KU" data-tag="01KU">26.21.12</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
monomorphism, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01L5" data-tag="01L5">26.23.4</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
surjective, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01S0" data-tag="01S0">29.9.2</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universally injective, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02V1" data-tag="02V1">29.10.5</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
affine, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01SC" data-tag="01SC">29.11.8</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
quasi-affine, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01SN" data-tag="01SN">29.13.4</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(locally) of finite type, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01T3" data-tag="01T3">29.15.3</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(locally) quasi-finite, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01TL" data-tag="01TL">29.21.12</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
(locally) of finite presentation, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01TR" data-tag="01TR">29.22.3</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
universally open, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02V2" data-tag="02V2">29.24.3</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
flat, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01U7" data-tag="01U7">29.26.6</a>, 
